theory.intro:
A protractor measures angles in degrees ($^{\circ}$). Lining it up correctly is the key to a correct reading.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (3,0) arc (0:180:3);
\draw (2.6,0) arc (0:180:2.6);
\draw (-3,0)--(3,0);
\foreach \a in {0,10,...,180}{\draw (\a:2.6)--(\a:3);}
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt);
\draw (0,-0.3)--(0,0.3);
\node[below,font=\small] at (2.85,-0.1) {$0$ or $180$};
\node[below,font=\small] at (-2.85,-0.1) {$180$ or $0$};
\node[below,font=\small] at (0,-0.7) {centre on the vertex};
\node[above,font=\small] at (0,3.1) {two scales};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
